survlearning includes the following upstream-derived numerical components.

Random survival forests
----------------------
Source: randomForestSRC 3.9.0, https://www.randomforestsrc.org/
Authors: Hemant Ishwaran and Udaya B. Kogalur.
License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
Upstream archive SHA256:
82E353BC2078C6EF1C4E7A08114192660281B7107C25431F30379C7FC74A2DE3

Files: src/rsf/* and R/rsf-core.R.
The numerical core is retained; native identifiers are isolated and registration
is provided by survlearning. R helpers are restricted to the fit/predict
dependency closure in a private environment. Browser-tree visualization,
external graphical dependencies and unrelated public interfaces are not exposed.
This is derived upstream software, not a claim of original algorithm authorship.

Royston-Parmar initialization and basis conventions
-------------------------------------------------
Source: flexsurv 2.3.2, https://github.com/chjackson/flexsurv
Authors: Christopher Jackson and contributors listed in that release.
License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
Upstream archive SHA256:
5B6705197A1B7C9F46BD7F4A02B3C66B4BA7EB413CDC0D649C6DA1D433AAE184

File: R/royston-parmar.R. The right-censored initialization is adapted from
flexsurv.splineinits and flexsurv.splineinits.cox. The same natural cubic spline
basis, event-time knot convention and BFGS fitting method are used. The focused
likelihood, derivatives and prediction implementation do not include the
general multistate, interval-censored or graphical interfaces of flexsurv.

Gehan elastic-net ADMM
---------------------
Source: penAFT 0.3.2, Aaron J. Molstad and Piotr M. Suder.
License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
Upstream archive SHA256:
5A2575DC83388FDE6BD51C6C23B7EC4B56CD5B532B8C91D9D7E00D6A70CA941D

Files: src/gehan.cpp and R/gehan.R. The scalar-penalty elastic-net path retains
the upstream pair ordering, leading-singular-value step bound, ADMM updates,
over-relaxation, adaptive rho and residual tolerances. Compressed adjacency
replaces dense n-by-n incidence lookup matrices without dropping any pairs or
observations. max_iter is honored (the upstream wrapper hard-codes 5000).
An exact sorted-residual objective and feasible dual lower bound are added.
Plotting, sparse-group penalties and separate cross-validation are not included.
